      {
        "DOI": "10.21203/rs.3.rs-8950363/v1",
        "title": [
          "TRNEWS-2025: A Large-Scale, Manually Annotated Turkish News Dataset for Text Classification and NLP Research"
        ],
        "issued": {
          "date-parts": [
            [
              2026,
              6,
              29
            ]
          ]
        },
        "is-referenced-by-count": 0,
        "abstract": "<title>Abstract</title>\n                <p>This study presents TRNEWS-2025, a labeled Turkish news dataset created for use in Turkish Natural Language Processing (NLP) and machine learning research. The TRNEWS-2025 dataset comprises news articles gathered from various Turkish online news sites and media portals up to the year 2025. It has been manually labeled under nine different categories: Magazine, Politics, Sports, Arts-Culture, Health, Finance-Economy, Science-Technology, Tourism, and Environment. The dataset aims to reflect real-world news language due to its diverse range of topics and up-to-date content.To evaluate the usability and distinctiveness of the dataset, experimental analyses were performed using BERT, a modern transformer-based model, and BiLSTM+GloVe, a classic deep learning architecture. The results show that the TRNEWS-2025 dataset can be used effectively with both model paradigms. The TRNEWS-2025 dataset aims to provide a reliable and up-to-date source dataset that can be utilized in various research areas, including Turkish text classification, topic identification, explainable artificial intelligence studies, and language model evaluations. The original contribution of a Turkish dataset, such as TRNEWS-2025, significantly provides up-to-date, comprehensive, and nine-class news data.</p>",
